 The staged consumer fixture retains its worker's exact env-exec lease receipt
 and actual typed retirement/cleanup snapshots in private evidence. Missing
 snapshots stay null; testcase success does not prove lease release or reaping.
+Persistent RCC reuse has a separate six-call staged test: results must count
+1 through 6 while worker and wrapper PID/create-time pairs, artifact,
+compatibility identity and receipt path stay fixed. The default one-call
+nonreuse test remains distinct. A matching wrapper alone does not identify the
+Action worker; require its measured PID ancestry, managed interpreter/Core
+origins and source hash. Synthetic poison/delegation controls prove validator
+sensitivity, not real reuse. Preserve the terminal raw lease and unknown
+cleanup fields; actual candidate qualification remains a separate gate.
 
 An isolated, sequential RCC qualification may share only its once-owned `pkgs`
 download cache between publication and staged execution for the same source and
